                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e0ac385-4d85-329f-a773-56fe583ca84a",
                        "entry_id": "383a3eb9-a6b8-3ad2-a534-4079eca999fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "склонность человека к принятию решений на основе собственной воли, в том числе вопреки здравому смыслу, мнению окружающих, соображениям законов, обычаев, правил и т. п."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0766d781-49b7-3dd1-9231-cf5c3a9bcfa6",
                        "entry_id": "383a3eb9-a6b8-3ad2-a534-4079eca999fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "поведение, поступки, свидетельствующие о склонности действовать по своей воле, прихоти"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3eb19515-a6f9-4fa4-8482-d5f02ea8b85d",
                                "sense_id": "0766d781-49b7-3dd1-9231-cf5c3a9bcfa6",
                                "text": "Таков беспорядок, зверство, своеволие и разврат русского суда и русской полиции, что простой человек, попавшийся под суд, боится не наказания по суду, а судопроизводства."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "22193f8b-714f-48f4-b4b2-9eed7f0473c6",
                        "source_entry_id": "383a3eb9-a6b8-3ad2-a534-4079eca999fa",
                        "target_lang_word": "obstinacy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "obstinacy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a812942-e87f-3ba9-a5dc-e0e0c2a494d3",
                                        "entry_id": "d2ea0fe7-e2ea-3927-a3b1-7f35fd6ee269",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state, or an act, of stubbornness or doggedness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67bf7caf-e589-46ea-bc2d-75c26c3b33bc",
                                                "sense_id": "0a812942-e87f-3ba9-a5dc-e0e0c2a494d3",
                                                "text": "He finished only through a mixture of determined obstinacy and ingenuity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfc6d731-a558-40c0-bc9b-07448a4f8211",
                                                "sense_id": "0a812942-e87f-3ba9-a5dc-e0e0c2a494d3",
                                                "text": "\"I don't know where,\" replied the girl.\n\"Then I do,\" said Sikes, more in the spirit of obstinacy than because he had any real objection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d76158a-f755-4db9-aa0c-13dffecb96b2",
                                                "sense_id": "0a812942-e87f-3ba9-a5dc-e0e0c2a494d3",
                                                "text": "1877, Leo Tolstoy (author), David Magarshack (translator), Anna Karenina, part 6, ch 12,\nHis hand closed, he drew back, and his face assumed a still more stubborn expression.\n\"For you it's a matter of obstinacy,\" she said, looking intently at him and suddenly finding the right word for the expression of his face which exasperated her so much."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f100f97-ad51-3850-ae39-effa6cd571db",
                                        "entry_id": "d2ea0fe7-e2ea-3927-a3b1-7f35fd6ee269",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of bison; the collective noun for bison."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "collective",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c640993-27ff-43f8-a458-ac876eabfdd7",
                        "source_entry_id": "383a3eb9-a6b8-3ad2-a534-4079eca999fa",
